Article 2: Commercial cases arising from the performance of duties by a futures exchange refer to:
(1) Commercial litigation cases brought by members of the futures exchange and their relevant personnel, margin depository banks and their relevant personnel, clients, and other futures market participants, on the grounds that the futures exchange, by violating laws, administrative regulations, and the provisions of the futures regulatory authority under the State Council, improperly performed its supervision and management duties and caused damage to them;
(2) Commercial litigation cases brought by members of the futures exchange and their relevant personnel, margin depository banks and their relevant personnel, clients, and other futures market participants, on the grounds that the futures exchange, by violating its charter, trading rules, implementation rules, and the terms of business agreements, improperly performed its supervision and management duties and caused damage to them;
(3) Other commercial litigation cases arising from a futures exchange's performance of duties.

Article 3: Where a futures exchange is the debtor, and a creditor requests the freezing or transfer of funds or securities in the following accounts, the People's Court shall not support:
(1) funds of members of the futures exchange in the margin accounts of the futures exchange;
(2) securities submitted by members of the futures exchange to the futures exchange for the purpose of offsetting margin.

Article 4: Where a futures company is the debtor, and a creditor requests the freezing or transfer of funds or securities in the following accounts, the People's Court shall not support:
(1) funds of clients in the margin accounts of the futures company;
(2) securities submitted by clients to the futures company for the purpose of offsetting margin.

Article 5: Where a clearing member of a futures exchange adopting the member-based tiered clearing system is the debtor, and a creditor requests the freezing or transfer of the following funds or securities of the clearing member, the People's Court shall not support:
(1) funds of non-clearing members in the margin accounts of the clearing member;
(2) securities submitted by non-clearing members to the clearing member for the purpose of offsetting margin.
